  "details": "the behavior is like this:\nlocally, if you have a world constraint with a child rigidbody, the child rigidbody will respect the world-fixedness of the constraint.\nremotely, if you have a world constraint with a child rigidbody, the rigidbody will move counter to your transforms\nif you put a world fixed joint(joint connected to none) on the world constraint, then locally the child rigidbody will act like a local object, and remotely it will respect the world-fixedness of the constraint + fixed joint\nthe working configuration is to locally animate is kinematic on, so the world fixed joint is inert, and animate it off remotely, so the world fixed joint is active\nsimply: \nWorld Constraint + Child Rigidbody: Works locally, broken remotely\nWorld Constraint + World Fixed Joint + Child Rigidbody: Broken locally, works remotely\nthis difference in the movement of rigidbodies is one of two reasons that avatar physics is broken, the other being the mirror collider issue.\n\nthis is a public avatar with the movement issue(there is no world fixed joint): https://vrchat.com/home/avatar/avtr_d2f04e8e-7196-44ee-a3c2-2701327a5244\n\nthis one doesn't have the issue(there is an animated world fixed joint): https://vrchat.com/home/avatar/avtr_ecd71bdd-f0d4-40ad-9e1b-35ee3985d564",
